  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "gf_sdp_info_parse",
    "file": "gpac/src/ietf/sdp.c",
    "description": "In the 'r' (repeat times) SDP line parsing branch, gf_sdp_info_parse writes to timing->OffsetFromStart[timing->NbRepeatOffsets] before enforcing the maximum bound. The check against GF_SDP_MAX_TIMEOFFSET happens only after increment, so when NbRepeatOffsets already equals the array size (10), it performs an out-of-bounds write/read index access at line 647. Root cause is incorrect bounds-check ordering in repeat-offset accumulation.",
    "conditions": "Input reaches rtpin_load_sdp -> gf_sdp_info_parse with an SDP containing a valid 't=' timing section followed by an 'r=' line that provides more than GF_SDP_MAX_TIMEOFFSET repeat-offset tokens (or enough malformed tokenization to keep producing tokens). Because timing is non-NULL after 't=', the parser enters case 'r' and repeatedly stores offsets; on the 11th offset it indexes OffsetFromStart[10] (array size 10), triggering UBSan OOB."
  },
